  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promotion of safe and fair labour migration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Office aims to align its work with key priorities of the Colombo Process and the objectives of the Global Compact for Migration (GCM), focusing on improving the recognition of skills and qualifications, ensuring fair recruitment practices, and supporting the sustainable reintegration of migrant workers. A key initiative in this effort is the expansion of the National Skills Passport, which will strengthen Pakistan&#x2019;s labour migration governance.

For the 2024&#x2013;2025 biennium, the project outlines several major goals. These include providing technical support for developing Bilateral Labour Agreements (BLAs), promoting fair recruitment practices while reducing recruitment costs, and assisting private employment agencies in adopting ethical business practices. The project also aims to raise awareness of the South Asia Qualification Referencing Framework to encourage regional standards, broaden the use of the National Skills Passport to include more Pakistani workers, and help the government explore and establish new migration corridors.</narrative>
  </description>
